    <description>A large member of the deer family, these extinct creatures once lived for millions of years before humans came into being. They subsist on tough grasses and similar foods, and prefer temperate regions of forests and plains.\n\nProtoceratids are rather nimble herbivores with an unusual feature on the males. While having the regular horns near the ears, males feature rostral horns above the nose covered in skin. These horns, which are fused at the base and branch at the tip, are likely used as a sexual display and also used in sparring for competition of mates.</description>
